This repository contains agent skills, reference documentation, golden test
fixtures, and CI tooling for analyzing and porting prebid-server bidder
adapters across language implementations.

The skills describe and ground patterns observed in:
  - prebid/prebid-server (https://github.com/prebid/prebid-server) — Apache License 2.0
  - prebid/prebid-server-java (https://github.com/prebid/prebid-server-java) — Apache License 2.0

The Adapter Specification format and the shared canonical references
(adapter-spec.md, behavior-taxonomy.md, port-translation-rules.md) describe
upstream behavior; they are derivative analytical works.

This repository redistributes upstream `static/bidder-params/{bidder}.json`
files byte-for-byte, under Apache License 2.0 from upstream. They are stored as
whole files in the content-addressed blob stores at

  prebid-server-go/read/test-fixtures/blobs/<sha256>
  prebid-server-java/read/test-fixtures/blobs/<sha256>

and each golden specification names the one it uses in `bidder_params_ref`
(`path`, `resolved_commit`, `sha256`, `bytes`), so every blob is traceable to
the upstream path and commit it was taken from. Before adapter_spec_version
2.0.0 the same bytes were transcribed into a `bidder_params_json` field inside
each golden; that field is gone and the blob store is the only copy.

PR numbers, file paths, maintainer contact addresses as they appear in upstream
bidder config, and behavioral observations quoted in this repository are taken
from public upstream sources. Individual reviewers' GitHub usernames are no
longer stored: the `cross_language.reviewer_cohort` field that held them was
removed at adapter_spec_version 2.0.0.
